.SH NAME
gyro-server-public-ip-get - Public IPv4 state


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBgyro server public-ip get  [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Public IPv4 state

.PP
Turning the public IPv4 off makes the server reachable only from its VPC, through a gateway port forward or with the web console (which always works). Confirm with the server's current IP (\fBconfirm_ip\fR). Needs a ready private card (409 \fBno_private_network\fR) and no additional IPv4 (409 \fBextra_ips\fR). If the VPC gateway (NAT) is off the server loses internet access: refused with 409 \fBno_egress\fR unless \fBallow_no_egress: true\fR\&. The address stays reserved for the server; turning it on brings the same IP.

.PP
API: GET /cloud/servers/{id}/public-ip (operationId getServerPublicIp, scope cloud_read)


